{{/*
  target-bead-header — the visible "target bead" preamble used by every
  beads-issues prompt that follows the flexible "linked bead OR fallback to
  the current conversation topic" convention (assess, discuss, investigate,
  resolved, status, work, mention-phase-*, mention-driver, and future
  consumers). Complements `_shared/beads/target-bead-header-strict.tmpl`,
  which is used by phase/driver prompts that REQUIRE a resolved target and
  bail via `mitto_ui_notify` when one is missing.

  Callers first resolve the target into a local `$target` variable, then
  invoke this fragment with a dict of parameters:

      {{ $target := "" -}}
      {{ if .Session.BeadsIssue }}{{ $target = .Session.BeadsIssue }}
      {{ else if .Args.IssueID }}{{ $target = .Args.IssueID }}{{ end -}}

      {{ template "_shared/beads/target-bead-header" (dict
          "Target"   $target
          "Noun"     "target bead"
          "Role"     "help the user **think through and refine** this bead ..."
          "NoTarget" "Help the user **think through and refine the current problem** ..."
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    Target   — the resolved bead ID (empty string when no bead is linked).
    Noun     — the noun used to refer to the bead (default: "target bead";
               callers use "target feature" / "target bug" / "target bead
               for this phase" depending on their family).
    Role     — the "Your job is …" clause that follows the "The <noun> is
               `<id>`." sentence. Optional; when empty the fragment emits
               just the terse "The <noun> is `<id>`." (matching `status`
               and `work`, whose per-step guidance follows immediately).
    NoTarget — the entire fallback paragraph rendered when Target is empty
               (starts after the required "There is **no linked bead** for
               this conversation." sentence, which the fragment always
               emits — pass just your prompt-specific continuation).

  The fragment renders one of two branches:
    * Target non-empty: "The <noun> is `<id>`.<Role>"
    * Target empty:     "There is **no linked bead** for this
                         conversation. <NoTarget>"

  It is self-contained (balanced `{{ if }}/{{ end }}`), so it is safe to
  invoke wherever a paragraph is expected in the caller.
*/}}
{{- $noun := "target bead" -}}
{{- with .Noun }}{{ $noun = . }}{{ end -}}
{{- if .Target -}}
The **{{ $noun }}** is `{{ .Target }}`.{{ with .Role }} {{ . }}{{ end }}
{{- else -}}
There is **no linked bead** for this conversation. {{ .NoTarget }}
{{- end }}
